				2515,
				66
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add Envelope.ChannelId, DashMap connection pool, and multiplexer reverse-RPC dispatch\n\nThree interconnected changes across the wire protocol, client concurrency model, and streaming multiplexer:\n\n**Proto — Envelope.ChannelId:** Add a `uint64 ChannelId = 5` field to the `Envelope` message, assigned by the side that owns the channel registry entry for this stream. Receivers compare this against the identifier observed at channel-open time to detect frames from a stale (pre-reconnect) channel. Zero signals no registry-assigned identifier. All multiplexer `Envelope` constructions set this to `0` — Mountain and Cocoon will populate it once the per-stream registry is wired.\n\n**Client — DashMap connection pool:** Replace `Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, CocoonClient>>>` with `dashmap::DashMap<String, CocoonClient>`, eliminating the single global lock on every `SendRequest`, `SendNotification`, and `DisconnectFromSideCar` call. All client site lock/unlock patterns collapse to direct `DashMap` method calls (`.get()`, `.insert()`, `.remove()`, `.contains_key()`). The `RecordSideCarFailure` eviction path similarly drops its explicit lock. Import `dashmap` in `Shared.rs`; no other dependency changes.\n\n**Multiplexer — reverse-RPC dispatch:** The `ReadPump` previously dropped inbound `Payload::Request` frames as a no-op with a comment reserving future dispatch. This commit wires full dispatch: a process-wide `REQUEST_HANDLER` storage (`Mutex<Option<RequestHandlerFn>>`) with an `InstallRequestHandler` public API that Mountain calls at gRPC-service construction time. Each inbound request spawns a `tokio::spawn` task invoking the handler, pushing the returned `GenericResponse` back over the stream sink under the original correlation id. If no handler is installed, the frame is dropped with a warning (preserving backward compatibility with the unary fallback). Cancellation frames remain dropped — the unary path has no cancellation either, so accepting and dropping preserves equivalence.\n\n**Doc polish:** Normalise line-wrapping across all 40+ notification atoms, Library.rs, Multiplexer.rs, and all Client files to a consistent column width. No behavioural changes in doc-only files.\n\nNo breaking changes — `ChannelId=0` is backward compatible, `DashMap` preserves the same `HashMap`-compatible API surface, and the multiplexer default handler is `None`.",
			"SHA": "e9d332c501a4ef2eebee6d05e58e0c3713c6fb02"
		},
